;; PgBouncer auth file. Format: "username" "password-hash-or-plaintext"
;;
;; Copy to deploy/pgbouncer/userlist.txt and replace "changeme" below with
;; the real `sirius` role's password -- the exact same value as
;; deploy/.env's own SIRIUS_DB_PASSWORD. deploy/pgbouncer/userlist.txt
;; is gitignored; only this .example file is committed.
;;
;; This governs pgbouncer's own outbound connection *to* Postgres, distinct
;; from pgbouncer.ini's auth_type (which governs the client-to-pgbouncer
;; leg only). A stale value here breaks every pooled DATABASE_URL connection
;; while DATABASE_DIRECT_URL (Alembic, which bypasses pgbouncer) keeps
;; working -- a real footgun documented in the GeM precedent this stack is
;; modeled on.
;;
;; Baked into the pgbouncer image at build time, so a password rotation
;; requires rebuilding the pgbouncer image, not merely restarting it.
"sirius" "changeme"
